 National Hindu Students’ Forum (UK) 
 “Preserving the Flame, Illuminating Tomorrow”
 The Diwali in London Committee brings together organisations from across the UK to organise and deliver this annual celebration. Each year, one organisation takes the lead as the Chair Organisation. For 2026, this is the National Hindu Students’ Forum (UK) (NHSF UK).
 Founded in 1991 by Hindu university students in London, NHSF (UK) exists to protect, preserve, practise and promote Hindu Dharma, creating spaces for young Hindus to explore their identity, build community and develop as future leaders and ambassadors.
 With a vision of a peaceful and harmonious world based on Dharma, NHSF (UK) engages young Hindus across schools and universities through cultural celebrations, discussions and debates, sports, arts, meditation and selfless service (sewā).
 This vision comes to life at Diwali on Trafalgar Square 2026, sharing the values of sewa, harmony and light with London’s diverse communities.
 Come and explore the history of NHSF (UK), discover how students have kept Hindu traditions alive for 35 years and see how Diwali is celebrated by Hindu students and communities across the UK! 
